  "content": {
    "title": "NY Mets vs Giants highlights: David Peterson dinged in loss",
    "text": "April 2, 2026Updated April 3, 2026, 2:19 a.m. ETSAN FRANCISCO – After a week full of empty offense, the Mets’ pitching joined in on the struggles in their series finale on Thursday night.David Peterson gave up five earned runs on nine hits and two walks and the Mets offense cooled off after a strong start in a 7-2 loss to the Giants at Oracle Park in San Francisco.After the Mets showed signs of life with a Bo Bichette RBI double in the opening inning, the Giants hit Peterson hard in the bottom of the frame. Luis Arraez ripped an RBI triple off the right-field wall and Matt Chapman gave the Giants the lead on an RBI double into the corner.Mark Vientos made a diving stop on Jung Hoo Lee but Peterson dropped the flip and another run scored.Vientos cut the Giants’ advantage to 3-2 with a solo home run off Robbie Ray, but the Giants piled on with two runs on four hits in the third inning.Sean Manaea made his first bulk bullpen appearance with mixed results. He gave up an RBI single to Casey Schmitt which was charged to Peterson and a solo home run to Rafael Devers in the sixth inning.Follow along for updates and analysis as the Mets and Giants open their series on Thursday night:Blade Tidwell shutting down former teamIn a bit of Mets nostalgia, the Giants recalled Blade Tidwell from Triple A and placed Jose Butto on the injured list with arm fatigue before Thursday's game.Tidwell came on in the seventh and worked around an infield single with two ground balls, including a double play. He also got Bo Bichette to line into an inning-ending double play in the eighth.Tidwell struck out a pair in the ninth inning to nail down his first career save.Rafael Devers tags home run off Sean ManaeaWhen Sean Manaea came into the game in the fifth inning, Harrison Bader narrowly missed a home run by a few feet.One inning later, Rafael Devers hit a center-cut fastball over the outstretched glove of Luis Robert Jr. into the first row of bleachers in left-center field. The Giants grew their lead to 7-2.Sean Manaea comes on in fifth inningDavid Peterson had appeared to settle in, working a 1-2-3 fourth inning with two strikeouts, but Carlos Mendoza came and got him at the first sign of trouble. That came after he issued a one-out walk to Jung Hoo Lee in the fifth inning.Sean Manaea came on for his first extended action, issued a one-out walk and a bloop single to Casey Schmitt that was charged to Peterson and gave the Giants a 6-2 lead.Peterson's second outing was a rough one. He gave up five earned runs on nine hits and two walks with five strikeouts in 4⅓ innings.David Peterson continues to be hit hard in third inningThe third inning spelled disaster for David Peterson.The Mets left-hander gave up three straight hits, including a swinging bunt by Matt Chapman to load the bases. Then, Jung Hoo Lee and Harrison Bader both hit sharp fly balls to center field for sacrifice flies that grew the Giants' edge to 5-2.The Giants loaded the bases again on a single and a walk but Peterson was able to strike out Willy Adames for the second time to stop the damage there.Mark Vientos belts first home run of 2026In a loaded infield, it has been hard for Mark Vientos to get everyday at-bats but he will certainly continue to get at-bats against left-handers.Vientos proved why on Thursday night as he belted a solo home run off Giants southpaw Robbie Ray on a 3-2 slider to lead off the second inning. It was Vientos' first of the 2026 season and got the Mets back within 3-2.David Peterson punished, loses lead in first inningIt only took one inning for the Giants to mount a response.The Giants jumped David Peterson in the bottom of the first inning. Luis Arraez tagged an RBI triple over the right-field wall and Matt Chapman followed it up with an RBI double into the right-field corner.Then, Peterson extended his rough opening frame with a catching error on a flip from Mark Vientos. It allowed Chapman to score from second base to move the Giants ahead 3-1.Bo Bichette breaks through for MetsThe offense has been hard to come by for the Mets over the last few games, but Bo Bichette helped matters in the top of the first inning.After Francisco Lindor was walked and then erased on a Juan Soto fielder's choice, Bichette laced an RBI double into left field to put the Mets ahead 1-0.It was Bichette's fourth RBI of the young season.What time is NY Mets vs SF Giants game today?Time: 9:45 p.m.How to watch NY Mets vs SF Giants game todayTV channel: SNY, MLB NetworkStreaming: MLB.TV for out of market viewersNY Mets, SF Giants starting pitchers todayMets: David Peterson (0-0, 0.00 ERA)Giants: Robbie Ray (0-1, 3.38 ERA)",
